      "headline": "Pension reform fallout: 40% of 2nd-pillar participants withdraw funds, spending boom documented",
      "summary": "Data showing approximately 40% of second-pillar pension fund participants have withdrawn their accumulated savings since the reform took effect triggered wide political debate; PM Ruginienė defended the reform and noted rising consumption with satisfaction, while President Nausėda discussed possible future flexibility on mandatory annuities and the Bank of Lithuania weighed in on system attractiveness. Analysts estimated roughly half the ~3 billion euros withdrawn was flowing into retail spending."
    },
    {
      "headline": "EU Cyprus summit triggers wide debate on Article 42.7 mutual defense clause and NATO's future",
      "summary": "The informal EU summit in Cyprus centered on clarifying the bloc's mutual defense clause (Article 42.7) amid US President Trump's criticism of NATO allies over the Iran war and a leaked Pentagon memo suggesting Spain could be suspended from NATO; EU leaders including Nausėda (covered separately in story 6) debated whether EU defense integration complements or risks undermining NATO, with Macron declaring the EU clause 'stronger' than NATO's Article 5."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Seimas approves new Kapčiamiestis military training ground and Tauragė range expansion despite local opposition",
      "summary": "Lithuania's parliament voted to establish a new military training facility at Kapčiamiestis (near the strategically vital Suwałki corridor) and to expand the existing Tauragė range into Jurbarkas district, overcoming objections from local residents and some within the governing coalition; the decisions were framed as responses to the deteriorating regional security environment."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lithuania's mandatory military draft expansion draws international attention",
      "summary": "Multiple international and domestic outlets covered Lithuania's recently reformed conscription policy expanding draft eligibility to all 18-to-22-year-old men; reporting noted a pragmatic rather than purely patriotic motivation among young Lithuanians, with volunteer numbers up sharply since 2022 and special operations forces also conducting intake selection."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ruginienė denies tasking foreign minister to arrange Trump meeting",
      "summary": "PM Ruginienė denied a media report that she had instructed Foreign Minister Kęstutis Budrys to arrange a meeting with US President Trump; she also denied having raised the matter through back channels and said the relationship with the president functions as a 'tandem.' The denials prompted further questions about her international ambitions and relationship with Budrys."
    },
    {
