      "summary": "NATO fighters including French Rafales based at Šiauliai Air Base in Lithuania intercepted Russian strategic bombers and fighter jets flying over the Baltic Sea; separately, Russia's Deputy Foreign Minister warned that European countries hosting French nuclear-capable Rafales would be added to priority target lists, with Lithuanian and Latvian presidents publicly engaging with the nuclear burden-sharing proposal."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lithuania's MoD moves to procure Merops anti-drone interceptors tested in Ukraine",
      "summary": "Lithuania's Ministry of Defence announced it is considering purchasing a test batch of Merops AS-3 Surveyor drone-intercepting systems without a standard tender, citing urgency; the system has been combat-tested in Ukraine and is described as compatible with Lithuania's existing air defense architecture."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nausėda calls for Rosatom sanctions on Chernobyl 40th anniversary",
      "summary": "On the 40th anniversary of the Chernobyl disaster, President Nausėda called for international sanctions against Russian nuclear energy company Rosatom, linking Russia's nuclear threats against Ukrainian nuclear facilities to the Chernobyl legacy; his call was noted internationally alongside similar commemorative events."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ruginienė calls for gender balance in diplomat appointments, criticizes Foreign Ministry",
      "summary": "PM Ruginienė publicly urged the Foreign Ministry to apply gender balance principles when appointing diplomats, in remarks that were interpreted by some as another sign of friction between the PM and Foreign Minister Budrys."
    },
    {
      "headline": "PM's official motorcade criticized for high-speed urban driving; Ruginienė pledges to moderate",
      "summary": "Conservative MP Mindaugas Lingė raised the issue of PM Ruginienė's escort convoy regularly speeding through Vilnius streets during a parliamentary Government Hour; Ruginienė acknowledged the criticism and promised to pay attention, in what became a minor public image episode."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Public trust poll shows Nausėda leading all figures; Ruginienė ranks tenth",
      "summary": "A new Baltic Surveys poll commissioned by ELTA found President Nausėda as the most trusted public figure in Lithuania at 10.4%, down from 13% in December; PM Ruginienė ranked tenth at 3.4%, while media figure Andrius Tapinas and Dawn of Nemunas leader Remigijus Žemaitaitis placed in the top rankings."
    }
  ]
}

